{"cluster_id": "C-2827", "topic": "Pool/CasMountRuntime owns mount fencing contract", "target": "architecture/mounts-and-leases", "member_ids": ["B017-103", "B018-037"], "canonical_claim": "`Pool/CasMountRuntime` owns mount fencing, lease keeping, self-remount state, writer epochs, build-sequence watermarks, active builds, `minActive`, and build-sequence allocation/retirement. `CasMountRuntime` owns mount fencing, the mount lease keeper, self-remount machinery, and build-sequence watermarks, while `CasStore` retains the `open` and `tryRemountOnce` orchestration and its claim\u2192ledger-quiesce\u2192fence-rearm order.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-16-cas-source-layout-refactoring.md#L535-L547", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-15-cas-source-layout-refactoring-design.md#casmountruntime"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2828", "topic": "The renewal fix is confined to", "target": "architecture/mounts-and-leases", "member_ids": ["B018-009"], "canonical_claim": "The renewal fix is confined to `CasServerRoot` and `MountLeaseKeeper`; it does not change generic or upstream ClickHouse code.", "issue_ids": ["#37"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-16-cas-merge-upload-retry-fix-design.md#fix-over-fencing"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2829", "topic": "T5 replaces deletion of the owner", "target": "architecture/mounts-and-leases", "member_ids": ["B021-018"], "canonical_claim": "T5 replaces deletion of the owner anchor with a conditional in-place tombstone rewrite using `Backend::putOverwrite` and the expected owner token; a successor that changes the object first makes the conditional write fail and the decommission tail aborts closed.", "issue_ids": ["T5"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-18-t5-owner-tombstone-design.md#L14-L24"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2830", "topic": "CAS recovery backoff must use condition_variable::wait_for", "target": "architecture/mounts-and-leases", "member_ids": ["B022-011"], "canonical_claim": "CAS recovery backoff must use `condition_variable::wait_for` tied to the pool shutdown event so pool teardown does not wait out the retry tail.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-20-cas-table-load-stuck-asyncloader-design.md#layer-1"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2831", "topic": "The rev.8 lifecycle has Running/live, transient-not-live", "target": "architecture/mounts-and-leases", "member_ids": ["B023-049"], "canonical_claim": "The rev.8 lifecycle has `Running/live`, `transient-not-live`, `IdentityLost`, `Vanished(replaced)`, and `Vanished(forgotten)` states; uncertain states throw, while only operator `FORGET` or foreign-pool proof supplies truthful absent answers.", "issue_ids": ["D5", "rev.8"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-22-cas-disk-lease-loss-throw-and-stop-verbs-design.md#L1-L38"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2832", "topic": "The rev.8 identity gate compares only", "target": "architecture/mounts-and-leases", "member_ids": ["B023-055"], "canonical_claim": "The rev.8 identity gate compares only `pool_id` and `blob_header_len`; successful decoding is the format gate, while `algos_used` and `min_reader_generation` are refreshed and never compared.", "issue_ids": ["B6", "rev.8"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-22-cas-disk-lease-loss-throw-and-stop-verbs-design.md#L49-L61"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2833", "topic": "The fence-not-rescue fix has three phases", "target": "architecture/mounts-and-leases", "member_ids": ["B024-082"], "canonical_claim": "The fence-not-rescue fix has three phases: exhaustive non-aborting classification in `MountLeaseKeeper::onRenewMismatch`, pre-I/O fence-deadline anchoring, and probe-gated writer-epoch re-minting with decommission-aware policy.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-24-cas-mount-lease-fence-not-rescue.md#L1-L18"]}
